   "unmapped": [
    "Arms are nodes of a known graph; features are rows of the Laplacian eigenvector matrix Q (ambient dimension D = N = K)",
    "Parameter is bounded in the spectral norm ||alpha||_Lambda = sqrt(alpha^T Lambda alpha) <= C with Lambda = Laplacian eigenvalues + lambda I",
    "The learner knows the graph Laplacian spectrum and an upper bound C on ||alpha*||_Lambda"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "In each time step $t\\le T$, the recommender $\\pi$ chooses a node $\\pi(t)$ and obtains a noisy reward such that: $r_t =\\langle \\bx_{\\pi(t)} , \\balpha^* \\rangle + \\varepsilon_t$, where the noise $\\varepsilon_t$ is assumed to be $R$-sub-Gaussian for any $t$. In our setting, we have $\\bx_v \\in \\R^D$ and $\\|\\bx_v\\|_2\\leq 1$ for all $\\bx_v$."
  }
